--- !u!114 &468685742
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 468685741}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 11ef4a55f472dae4498976f5ec94cb09, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  allDialogues:
  - lines:
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: Demon, where am I?
    - speakerName: Demonio
      text: You know I have a name, right?
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: I don't care, answer the question.
    - speakerName: Demonio
      text: How sharp. You should have better manners, especially if you're asking
        me for things.
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: If you don't answer me, I'll kill you.
    - speakerName: Demonio
      text: Kill me? I'm already dead, dear. And if you did, or could, you would
        be alone in hell with no company, at the mercy of the demons.
    - speakerName: Demonio
      text: Unfortunately, we need each other. You need me as much as I need you.
        So be nice, or I won't answer.
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: ...
    - speakerName: Demonio
      text: 'Come on, I''m just asking you to be nice. You can do it. Just call me
        by my name: Alastor.'
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: Alastor... Where are we?
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: We are in Gluttony, the ring of voracious appetite and the greatest hunger.
        That wasn't so difficult, was it?
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "Shut up, Alastor.\r"
  - lines:
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: Is that the exit?
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: It seems so. The bridge connects to the king's garden here.
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: King? Do you mean Lucifer?
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: No, Lucifer is the king of all hell. Fortunately, he should be in Pride.
        I mean Beelzebub, a sin. He is inferior to Lucifer and only rules Gluttony.
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: King of hell? Sins that rule rings?
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: 'Didn''t they tell you? It''s not hard to understand. The rings are ruled
        by sins: Beelzebub rules Gluttony, Asmodeus rules Lust, Lucifer rules Pride,
        and the list goes on until 9, or well... 7...'
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "Lucifer is a sin, but he is still the damned king of all hell and its
        souls...\r"
  - lines:
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "Alastor, tell me something.\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "You finally want me to tell you my story, don't you? You can't resist
        the temptation of your new partner.\r"
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "No. How do I get to Pride?\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "Boring. That's easy, dear. Knock on the gates of Hell and kill its rulers.
        Their deaths will make you strong. Fight your way through until you reach
        our king.\r"
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "Is there no way to avoid them? A shortcut?\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "Won't you wield your sword? How will you kill them? Appeal to their
        compassion? Say pretty words and resolve it with talk?\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: 'I''m sure they''ll open the gates of the ring for you after a farewell
        hug. Oh, how sweet, you really are a saint, believing that demons can be
        saved. You''re so pure that you don''t deserve to be down here.

'
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "Don't be an idiot. They'll kill you and do whatever they want with your
        corpse. They'll cut you open from here to here, golden blood is highly coveted
        here. All the rings have plans for you. I bet all of Gluttony and Lust would
        fight just to possess you in many unimaginable ways, all twisted and agonising.
        An opera of screams and a melody of cries.\r"
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "Answer my question, demon. If I die, you die, you have no choice.\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: "That's what you think, sweetheart. I didn't survive this long by being
        like the other filthy, despicable beings. But unless your wings grow back,
        you will fight, you will kill them, and you will give me the blood of the
        damned sinners.\r"
    - speakerName: Faith
      text: "Do you want their power? Do you hold a grudge against them for something?
        Or is it both?\r"
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: ...
    - speakerName: Alastor
      text: I don't want to tell my story anymore...
  dialogueSystem: {fileID: 468685744}
  maxUnlockedBlocks: 0
  currentBlock: 0
